    "body": "With low values you can have a big animal right by you and not be studying it even when your crosshair is right on it. I'm assuming this is because you're checking against the animal's registration point and not its hitbox or something? Perhaps we should move on to a raycast-based version: you set the % of your screen width as a radius. It draws a circle around y our crosshair when in aiming/bino mode. It casts rays within that circle. Not just on the center and edge. Number of rays unknown. Performance implications? Returns animals/herbs hit. Studies them. Feasible?",
